    "q-162394": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162394",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let $E$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ that satisfy $f(0)=1.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. The exponential function $f(x)={e}^{x}\\in E$\n\nII. For any $f(x),g(x)\\in E$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in E.$\n\nIII. The set $E$ is closed under addition.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that\n\n$$\nf(0)={e}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, $f\\in E.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the function $f(x)=g(x)={e}^{x}\\in E.$ Then, \n\n$$\n(f+g)(0)={e}^{0}+{e}^{0}=1+1=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)+g(x)\\notin E.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $E$ is not closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
